Limitations

| Limitation                | Description                                 |
| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| Learning curve            | More concepts than a simple chain           |
| Additional design effort  | Requires planning of nodes and state        |
| Overkill for simple tasks | Not necessary for straightforward workflows |
| State management          | Poorly designed state can become complex    |


=======

LangGraph is a framework for building stateful, graph-based AI workflows.
It extends LangChain with multi-agent orchestration, conditional routing, loops, and shared state.
It is particularly useful for applications such as booking systems, customer support, research assistants, 
and other complex workflows where multiple steps, decisions, and retries are required.
For your multi-agent bus ticket booking chatbot, LangGraph is a strong fit because it can coordinate specialised 
agents (search, booking, payment, notifications) while maintaining a consistent state throughout the conversation.

